<title>USA: Sears, Roebuck unit sells $300 mln notes.</title>
<headline>Sears, Roebuck unit sells $300 mln notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Sears Roebuck Acceptance Corp, a unit of Sears, Roebuck and Co, was priced on Tuesday via Morgan Stanley &amp; Co, according to market sources.</p>
<p>BORROWER SEARS ROEBUCK ACCEPTANCE CORP</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 6.95 PCT   MATURITY 5/15/2002</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.808  FIRST PAY DATE 11/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD 6.996 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD +45 BP     CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
